("ADJ-147","unique – (not usually compared)","'Unique' means one of a kind, so 'most unique' is avoided. Say 'truly unique'.","UNI-QUE: UNI = one.","Indian English often uses 'unique' for 'unusual'; standard English is stricter.","Write a sentence about something unique about your hometown.",None,"unique vs rare","Rare = few exist. Unique = only one exists."),
